From 66e9d4b9ef0ff5b2ad5e6b00d1afc8dfb70949d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:02:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] model.options: one pool and auth-store read per
 provider per picker build (card J rpc_dispatch)

Design t_01a1d563 card J, rpc_dispatch row (2.2 -> <=1.0% of a core). Hub P1 (serve
1257536 / 1316938): rpc/model.options 0.40-0.62% (158-210 ms CPU per call, ~11 calls per
400 s), the top method. In the hub profile (cardJ/sv2.raw) load_pool is 27 of the 39
samples under model.options: one picker build asks about the same pool from the raw-pool,
overlay and canonical sections, ~80 full load_pool reads for ~47 providers, and every
read-only auth check re-parses the 29 KB auth.json.

- list_authenticated_providers runs inside picker_build_scope(): a ContextVar memo that
  lives for ONE build only. _credential_pool_is_usable shares the build's load_pool result
  per provider; _auth_store_has_provider / _raw_pool_usable share one auth.json parse
  while the file's version is unchanged (a load_pool seed that persists mid-build is
  re-read by the next check). Nothing is cached across calls, so a credential added,
  removed or exhausted is seen by the next build; nested scopes reuse the outer memo, and
  the parallel prefetch threads (no context) load afresh as before.
- A pool load error is not memoized and still falls back to raw_pool_present.

profiles.list (0.22%) is ~70% _check_gateway_running in the hub profile; #2634 memoizes
that. shell.exec (0.42-0.48%) is the user's own command plus output redaction, which is a
security path: left as is.

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_picker_pool_memo.py): RED on base 5/5 (83 pool loads for 47
providers per build; replay 150-188 ms per call = 0.41-0.52% of a core at the hub rate vs
the 0.3% budget; the scope API is new). GREEN: replay 82-89 ms per call (best of 5) =
0.22-0.24%; 147 picker/inventory tests across 23 files pass.
